That's *quite* wrong. Magic resistance protects against a whole lot of
nasty stuff reflection doesn't. Including some insta-deaths and spells
that are almost always effectively insta-deaths. It also makes
teleport and level teleport traps much less dangerous (incl. less risk
of loosing your pet, which is admitedly not very important for
samurai).

I do believe that one should think about strategy early on, esp. in
this case, so one should also consider that getting magic resistance
is not very likely to happen further on (unless you wish for it from
the castle wand or get it with your quest artifact, but I'd consider
both variants too late).

